    "text": "Yes, education needs its content and process to include all three: right understanding in the self, relationships with human beings, and physical facility with nature.\n\nEvaluation of present education:\nPresent education largely focuses on physical facility, technical skills, and material accumulation. As a result, it leads to living in animal consciousness, where physical facility is treated as adequate, leaving human relationships and inner self-understanding neglected.\n\nThe way forward:\nThe way forward is to reorient education-sanskar towards holistic development, facilitating the transformation from animal consciousness to human consciousness. This requires placing right understanding first, followed by right relationships, and lastly physical facility in proper priority to ensure continuous happiness and prosperity for all.",
    "style_clone_from": {
      "adapter": "docx",
      "payload": {
        "v": 1,
        "kind": "paragraph",
